From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: fall back to the SPI flash environment

With the environment only in SPI flash (ENV_IS_IN_FAT disabled, as
in netcube_kumquat_defconfig), a boot from any source other than SPI
finds no location: env_get_location() returns ENVL_UNKNOWN at prio 0,
so env_init() fails and, by the code, U-Boot hangs before the console
is up.

Use the SPI flash environment as the last fallback, after FAT and UBI.
Configurations with FAT or UBI behave as before.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -138,6 +138,7 @@ void i2c_init_board(void)
  * If the raw MMC environment is also enabled, this is tried next.
  * When booting from NAND we try UBI first, then NAND directly.
  * SPI flash falls back to FAT (on SD card).
+ * Otherwise the first enabled of FAT, UBI and SPI flash is used.
  */
 enum env_location env_get_location(enum env_operation op, int prio)
 {
@@ -179,14 +180,16 @@ enum env_location env_get_location(enum env_operation op, int prio)
 	 * environment location other than ENVL_UNKNOWN, or the setup sequence
 	 * in board_f() will silently hang. This is arguably a bug in
 	 * env_init(), but for now pick one environment for which we know for
-	 * sure to have a driver for. For all defconfigs this is either FAT
-	 * or UBI, or NOWHERE, which is already handled above.
+	 * sure to have a driver for. For all defconfigs this is either FAT,
+	 * UBI or SPI flash, or NOWHERE, which is already handled above.
 	 */
 	if (prio == 0) {
 		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT))
 			return ENVL_FAT;
 		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_UBI))
 			return ENVL_UBI;
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_SPI_FLASH))
+			return ENVL_SPI_FLASH;
 	}
 
 	return ENVL_UNKNOWN;
